From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:00:00 +0000
Subject: wireless: uwe5622: do not read the station index of a command

sprdwl_tx_msg_func() calls prepare_addba() for every message. For a
command the buffer holds no tx_msdu_dscr, so sta_lut_index is a command
byte and intf->tx_num[] is read out of bounds:

  BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in sprdwl_tx_msg_func+0xeb0/0x13a0 [sprdwl_ng]
  Read of size 8 at addr ffff0000109d5900 by task kworker/u17:0/122
   sprdwl_send_cmd+0x6c/0x140 [sprdwl_ng]
   sprdwl_cmd_send_to_ic+0x11c/0x3a0 [sprdwl_ng]
   sprdwl_cmd_send_recv+0x300/0xf60 [sprdwl_ng]
   sprdwl_set_mc_filter+0xe0/0x160 [sprdwl_ng]

prepare_addba() does nothing without a peer entry, which only data
messages have. Call it only then.

Upstream: to be submitted to https://github.com/armbian/uwe5622
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/tx_msg.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/tx_msg.c b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/tx_msg.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/tx_msg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/tx_msg.c
@@ -1310,8 +1310,9 @@ int sprdwl_tx_msg_func(void *pdev, struc
 	if (msg->msg_type != SPRDWL_TYPE_DATA)
 		sprdwl_queue_msg_buf(msg, msg->msglist);
 
-	prepare_addba(intf, dscr->sta_lut_index, (struct sk_buff *)msg->skb,
-			 peer_entry, tid);
+	if (peer_entry)
+		prepare_addba(intf, dscr->sta_lut_index,
+			      (struct sk_buff *)msg->skb, peer_entry, tid);
 
 	if (msg->msg_type == SPRDWL_TYPE_CMD)
 		tx_up(tx_msg);
